0..76 Comment "// Two proofs by induction over the presented circle that prove nothing. The"
77..150 Comment "// first forgets to carry the loop: its loop arm answers with the field\'s"
151..227 Comment "// path, whose endpoints are not the loop\'s. The second carries the loop but"
228..300 Comment "// answers the inverse apart, so the two sides of a cancellation are two"
301..320 Comment "// different paths."
322..373 Comment "/// The circle, presented by its two cancellations."
